  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "1v1 through the gate",
  "description": "A small box of about 5 × 5 metres with a gate of two cones, one metre apart, in the middle. Two players face each other 1v1 with one ball. Whoever has the ball scores a point each time they carry it through the gate – from either direction. The other tries to win the ball and then attacks themselves.\n\nPlay for about a minute, then change opponents so the games stay even. At a higher level, play 2v2 in the same box. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "If the gate is shut from one side – switch sides and come in from the other."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use your body between the opponent and the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defender: stand between the ball and the gate, not behind the gate."
    }
  ],
